---
title: CLI vs GUI vs Python
sidebar:
  order: 3
---

SEGUL comes in three interfaces: a **graphical user interface (GUI)**, a **command-line interface (CLI)**, and a **Python library (PySEGUL)**. Every interface runs the same genomic tools and is self-contained. You can install one or all and switch at any time.

| | GUI | CLI | Python |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| How you use it | Point and click | Commands and scripts | Python code |
| Best for | Most users, teaching, phones | Pipelines and HPC clusters | Python workflows |
| Install | [App stores](/docs/installation/install_gui/) | [Pre-built binary, Bioconda, Cargo](/docs/installation/install_cli/) | [`pip install pysegul`](/docs/api-usage/python/intro/) |
| Runs on | Desktop, tablet, phone | Linux, macOS, Windows, WSL | Linux, macOS, Windows, WSL |
| Requires | Nothing else | Nothing else | Python 3.10+ |
| Charts and reports | Built-in viewer | `--plot` option | [`PlotOptions` and report loaders](/docs/api-usage/python/plots_reports/) |

{% interfaceoverview /%}

## Platform support

{% platformmatrix /%}

See the [GUI](/docs/installation/install_gui/) and [CLI](/docs/installation/install_cli/#pre-compiled-binary) installation guides. For Linux, the CLI comes as a fully static binary for older distributions and a GLIBC-linked binary for newer ones. You can also [build the CLI from source](/docs/installation/install_cli/#source-code).

## Features

{% featuresplit /%}

Each GUI task group maps to one or more CLI commands:

{% commandmap /%}

Each CLI command also has a PySEGUL class, for example `segul align concat` is `AlignmentConcatenation`. See the [full list](/docs/api-usage/python/intro/#available-features).

Learn more about the [CLI](/docs/cli-usage/command_options/), [GUI](/docs/gui-usage/intro/), and [Python](/docs/api-usage/python/intro/) options.

## Performance

The charts below are built from the [SEGUL benchmark data](https://github.com/hhandika/segul-bench) (SEGUL v0.20.0). Desktop runs used Linux on an AMD Ryzen 9 5900X. [AMAS](https://github.com/marekborowiec/AMAS) and [goalign](https://github.com/evolbioinfo/goalign) are included for comparison. The [SEGUL paper](https://doi.org/10.1111/1755-0998.13964) describes the methods.

